API-13: validate the new REPORTSTART value; no statistic for no periods

EN_settimeparam(EN_REPORTSTART) tested the current report start against
the duration instead of the new value. A start after the end of the run
was accepted, and from then on every valid value was refused with 213.
Test the new value. A run that reports no period at all (for example one
that halts before REPORT START) also made savetimestat() divide the
STATISTIC AVERAGE sums by zero periods and write NaN to the output file.
Skip the statistic when there is no period, as the SERIES case already
writes no results then.

Apply from the root of an EPANET checkout at 83e25bb:
    git apply API-13_fix.patch

diff --git a/src/epanet.c b/src/epanet.c
index 47dc1e4..0163edf 100644
--- a/src/epanet.c
+++ b/src/epanet.c
@@ -1692,7 +1692,7 @@ int DLLEXPORT EN_settimeparam(EN_Project p, int param, long value)
         break;
 
     case EN_REPORTSTART:
-        if (time->Rstart > time->Dur) return 213;
+        if (value > time->Dur) return 213;
         time->Rstart = value;
         break;
 
diff --git a/src/output.c b/src/output.c
index 5ecd743..1f11340 100644
--- a/src/output.c
+++ b/src/output.c
@@ -630,7 +630,9 @@ int savefinaloutput(Project *pr)
     FILE *outFile = out->OutFile;
 
     // Save time series statistic if computed
-    if (rpt->Tstatflag != SERIES && out->TmpOutFile != NULL)
+    // (there is none if no time period was reported)
+    if (rpt->Tstatflag != SERIES && out->TmpOutFile != NULL &&
+        rpt->Nperiods > 0)
     {
         x = (REAL4 *)calloc(MAX(net->Nnodes, net->Nlinks) + 1, sizeof(REAL4));
         if (x == NULL) return 101;
